<title>CUBA: Cuba, Bosnia-Herzegovina establish diplomatic ties.</title>
<headline>Cuba, Bosnia-Herzegovina establish diplomatic ties.</headline>
<dateline>HAVANA 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cuba and Bosnia-Herzegovina have established diplomatic relations, the official Cuban newspaper Granma said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The paper, mouthpiece of Cuba's ruling Communist Party, said the agreement was signed on Tuesday by the two countries' ambassadors in the Austrian capital Vienna.</p>
<p>Communist-ruled Cuba also has diplomatic relations with Croatia and the rump state of Yugoslavia.</p>
</text>
